  "headline": "Metoprolol succinate is not on FDA's shortage list as of 2026-10-21; Teva Pharmaceuticals USA, Inc. posted a discontinuation on 2026-08-31",
  "headline_cites": ["D5", "E24"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's drug shortage list shows metoprolol succinate is not listed as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["D5"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Teva Pharmaceuticals USA, Inc. posted a discontinuation for metoprolol succinate extended-release tablets on 2026-08-31, citing a business decision to discontinue manufacture.",
      "cites": ["E24"]
    },
    {
      "text": "NuCare Pharmaceuticals, Inc. (FEI 3003294404) is a registered repack plant for a metoprolol succinate label; its last inspection was classified NAI on 2025-03-12.",
      "cites": ["E11"]
    },
    {
      "text": "NuCare Pharmaceuticals, Inc. received a Warning Letter on 2019-09-27 and multiple VAI inspections from 2010 through 2020.",
      "cites": ["E5", "E6", "E7", "E9", "E10"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Bryant Ranch Prepack (FEI 1000519407) is a registered relabel/repack plant for a metoprolol succinate label; its last inspection was classified VAI on 2026-07-16.",
      "cites": ["E23"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Bryant Ranch Prepack had an OAI inspection in 2009, a Warning Letter in 2010, and subsequent VAI inspections through 2026.",
      "cites": ["E13", "E14", "E15", "E16", "E17", "E18", "E19", "E20", "E21", "E22"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule-based best option is to buy from Actavis Pharma, Inc., which is not on FDA's shortage list today, though its label names no plant we could place.",
      "cites": ["D6"]
    }
  ]
}
